      {
        "id": 198411,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-05-25T02:54:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Adam\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/adam/48/1946_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Adam:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>2. Christopher says that the art on cards does go with at least the issue number from the flavor text, during the discussion about when they build Freedom Tower.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>No, not always. We’ve said as much before, while they often are linked, it’s not all of them.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That’s why it jumped out at me. I may have read too much into an offhand comment, though.</p>\n<p>… Having finished the episode, I think now I’ve heard a good reason to get my hands on the RPG starter kit instead of waiting for the full book to come out! Sounds like there will be lots of good story bits, and good character stuff.</p>\n<p>So, funny story: in my line of work, we often have to deal with really old stuff. Like, computer code written in the mid-90s. Sometimes, it’s a huge burden to deal with. But we can’t escape it, because once something works in flight it’s basically made of solid gold - we say it has “flight heritage.” I was complaining to a colleague once about how heritage code is awful. He said, “Oh, no, heritage stuff is great! It’s <em>legacy</em> code that’s terrible!”</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:26:20.081Z",
