      {
        "id": 198412,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-05-25T05:05:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wasn't sure whether they were counting Felicia, but they did say \"all new heroes.\" &nbsp;Although it's also not 100% clear that Daybreak and the default hero team are one and the same.If Felicia is part of the team, though, she's a FISS through-and-through. &nbsp;FISSes frequently have oddball powers thrown into their mix, but like her laser eyes, they're typically single-purpose. &nbsp;True Blasters, like Ra and Tempest, are more versatile with their attack powers, being able to shape and control the energies they unleash in a wide range of different ways for different purposes. &nbsp;The Atomic Glare seems to be purely a point-and-shoot deal.Good thought on Daybreak being former Citizens of the Sun. &nbsp;It would make perfect sense for a junior powered team suddenly coming from nowhere and working together right off the bat, and of course \"breaking away from the Sun\" is a perfect description.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What is a FISS?</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
